1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,240
Hi, Neil. How are you doing?

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,340
I'm very well. Thank you, Georgie. How are you?

3
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:04,860
I'm very well too.

4
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:08,660
Neil, in this episode of Real Easy English,

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,980
we're talking about complaining.

6
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:14,620
That is when you say something is wrong

7
00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:17,560
or you have a problem and you want to tell someone about it.

8
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:20,300
Yes, and people should remember that they can get

9
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:25,280
a free worksheet for this podcast at bbclearningenglish.com.

10
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:35,880
I know that you have a recent experience with this, don't you?

11
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:41,440
Ah, yes. Yeah. I booked somewhere to stay on a trip

12
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:43,580
and the reviews were all really good.

13
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:46,980
And then when I checked again, the reviews were all really bad.

14
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:48,940
Oh, no. What were they about?

15
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:52,180
They said the place was dirty and things were broken.

16
00:00:52,620 --> 00:00:56,420
Oh, no. What did you do? Have you been yet?

17
00:00:56,680 --> 00:00:58,500
Not yet. Oh. No.

18
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:00,080
So what did you do?

19
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:04,620
I wrote to them. I sent them an email to say, I was worried.

20
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:11,440
And I asked them to assure me that the place would be clean

21
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:13,140
and working properly.

22
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:15,480
OK. And did you get a response?

23
00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:19,860
I did. But I really hated the whole process.

24
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:21,860
Oh, no. Why?

25
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:23,680
Because I don't like complaining.

26
00:01:24,140 --> 00:01:26,700
No, neither do I. I'm not very good at it.

27
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:30,360
I don't like to make people feel bad, even if there is a problem

28
00:01:30,360 --> 00:01:34,940
and I've paid for something, and it should be a certain way,

29
00:01:34,940 --> 00:01:35,740
but it's not.

30
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:39,360
And I'm entitled to complain.

31
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:41,260
I still don't like it.

32
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:44,620
I just feel, yeah, I feel embarrassed about it.

33
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:47,080
Yeah. It's not an easy thing to do.

34
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:51,540
No. I think I'm getting better with age, I think.

35
00:01:51,720 --> 00:01:52,820
I'm getting braver.

36
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:59,620
I had an experience a couple of weeks ago because I am subscribed

37
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:02,260
to a food delivery service.

38
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:04,840
I get a box of food every week.

39
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:09,820
And the last two weeks, the delivery has been very late.

40
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:11,520
And I'm not happy about it.

41
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:18,480
And so I found the courage, found the bravery to call up the customer

42
00:02:18,480 --> 00:02:20,740
service and complain.

43
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:27,220
And I was very strong and I asked for money, a discount on the next order.

44
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:30,700
Wow. That sounds very well done.

45
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:37,600
I think when you do complain, sometimes you feel bad about it.

46
00:02:37,660 --> 00:02:43,800
But if it works out well, like with you, and hopefully with my accommodation,

47
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:50,620
afterwards you feel really good because you did what was right.

48
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:56,060
Yeah. If you've paid for something, I think you can expect it to be what you

49
00:02:56,060 --> 00:03:00,820
paid for. So if it isn't, I think you're allowed to complain.

50
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:03,320
But there is a nice way to do it, isn't there?

51
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:06,560
There is. Yeah. Be polite. Don't be personal.

52
00:03:07,720 --> 00:03:12,620
It's not often the person you are complaining to is often not the person

53
00:03:12,620 --> 00:03:15,740
responsible for the mistake or whatever.

54
00:03:15,740 --> 00:03:20,200
Yeah. So I think if you are respectful and polite,

55
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:22,080
but you know what you want.

56
00:03:22,620 --> 00:03:26,840
So Neil, you and I find complaining quite stressful.

57
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:31,780
So we don't do it very often. But do you know anyone that complains all the time?

58
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:38,740
Oh, yeah. Some people seem to love complaining and they complain about things

59
00:03:38,740 --> 00:03:40,980
that I would not complain about.

60
00:03:41,620 --> 00:03:46,320
Yeah. I've been in restaurants with groups of people where there's been someone

61
00:03:46,320 --> 00:03:49,980
that has complained about something that is really embarrassing.

62
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:53,200
And you just think this is not a real big issue.

63
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:55,160
Has that ever happened to you?

64
00:03:55,520 --> 00:04:00,140
Yeah. The same thing. I've been having a meal with some friends.

65
00:04:00,580 --> 00:04:04,260
One of the people I was with, he used to be a waiter.

66
00:04:04,880 --> 00:04:09,660
And he had a very clear idea about how waiters should behave.

67
00:04:09,660 --> 00:04:13,780
And he didn't like something and he complained about it.

68
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:19,200
And nobody else really understood what he was talking about or why he was complaining.

69
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:20,580
And it was embarrassing.

70
00:04:21,060 --> 00:04:24,660
Did he complain to the waiter? Yeah. But so everyone could hear.

71
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,920
Oh, no. And how did the waiter respond?

72
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:31,080
I don't think he liked it very much.

73
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:34,160
Well, I used to work in restaurants.

74
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:37,880
I've also worked in customer service. But in restaurants,

75
00:04:38,640 --> 00:04:43,920
if people have a reason to complain, of course, I'm going to try to fix it.

76
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:47,960
But it also depends how they say it.

77
00:04:48,740 --> 00:04:54,720
If they're very rude, as a waitress, you don't really want to help them.

78
00:04:55,340 --> 00:04:58,520
But if they're polite and they have a reason to complain, of course,

79
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:01,060
I'll try to fix their problems.

80
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:12,480
Okay, Neil, it's time to recap the vocabulary we used in this conversation.

81
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:18,220
We used the verb complain, which is when you say something is wrong or not good enough.

82
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:20,560
And we also heard the noun complaint.

83
00:05:21,140 --> 00:05:23,360
We did. And you make a complaint, don't you?

84
00:05:23,700 --> 00:05:28,700
Yes. We also heard discount, which is when you don't pay the full price of something.

85
00:05:29,260 --> 00:05:32,880
You also said that people are entitled to something,

86
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:37,720
and it means that that is something they should get if they paid for it.

87
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:43,940
And Neil, you said you were worried about the reviews of the accommodation for your trip,

88
00:05:44,340 --> 00:05:47,480
which is when people write what they think about the place.

89
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:49,940
That's it then, Georgie. Isn't it?

90
00:05:50,540 --> 00:05:53,260
But join us again another time for more Real Easy English.

91
00:05:53,640 --> 00:05:56,600
Don't forget there's a free worksheet on the website. Goodbye for now.

92
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:57,040
Goodbye.
